WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.893
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.163 --> 00:19.416
[theme music playing]

3
00:26.674 --> 00:28.551
[liquid bubbling]

4
00:32.888 --> 00:35.558
[clinking, rattling]

5
00:35.641 --> 00:36.684
[cat meows]

6
00:37.643 --> 00:39.478
[hoofbeats]

7
00:41.397 --> 00:42.273
[water splashes]

8
00:49.238 --> 00:51.156
[handcuffs rattling, click]

9
00:55.619 --> 00:57.037
[Jae-hee grunts] Get back here!

10
00:57.955 --> 01:00.541
-You sneaky little sneaker! -[Jerry meowing]

11
01:00.624 --> 01:02.209
Meow!

12
01:04.128 --> 01:05.838
Come back, Yi-jun Junior!

13
01:11.176 --> 01:12.261
[chuckles]

14
01:14.722 --> 01:16.390
Eh? [soft chuckle]

15
01:21.353 --> 01:22.605
Junior!

16
01:22.688 --> 01:23.898
[Jerry meows]

17
01:29.194 --> 01:30.696
[soft sigh]

18
01:30.779 --> 01:33.949
I've never seen anyone act like that while they were drunk.

19
01:34.617 --> 01:35.576
Whatever.

20
01:40.539 --> 01:41.707
What if he hurts himself?

21
01:42.750 --> 01:44.001
Who would take care of me?

22
01:51.091 --> 01:52.551
No one forced him to get drunk.

23
01:53.719 --> 01:55.095
[tuts, inhales]

24
01:55.596 --> 01:56.513
Hey!

25
01:57.014 --> 01:57.848
Wait, what?

26
01:58.349 --> 01:59.350
[Jae-hee] What the heck?

27
02:00.184 --> 02:03.562
Ah, seriously, what are you doing? [grunts]

28
02:04.313 --> 02:05.314
[grunts]

29
02:06.357 --> 02:07.733
-Whoa! -[grunts]

30
02:08.400 --> 02:09.985
S-Special Forces, you…

31
02:10.069 --> 02:11.028
[groaning]

32
02:11.403 --> 02:13.572
-Get off me! -[groans]

33
02:13.656 --> 02:15.741
-[panting] -[Jae-hee groans]

34
02:16.325 --> 02:17.326
[angry huff]

35
02:17.409 --> 02:19.161
[breathes angrily]

36
02:19.954 --> 02:21.664
[panting]

37
02:23.374 --> 02:24.291
Get back here!

38
02:27.544 --> 02:29.421
-[whimsical music playing] -[water splashing]

39
02:29.505 --> 02:30.798
[whimpering]

40
02:30.881 --> 02:31.715
[tinks]

41
02:33.634 --> 02:36.553
[birds chirping]

42
02:38.430 --> 02:41.058
[Yi-jun inhales, exhales]

43
02:46.689 --> 02:48.107
[Jae-hee] I mean, who the hell hits someone

44
02:48.190 --> 02:50.109
then just makes a run for it? Damn it.

45
02:56.115 --> 02:57.866
[heart pounding]

46
03:02.287 --> 03:04.498
[dreamy music playing]

47
03:09.837 --> 03:11.922
[breathing heavily]

48
03:19.304 --> 03:22.307
[breathing deeply]

49
03:22.683 --> 03:24.852
[breathing heavily]

50
03:24.935 --> 03:26.186
[Jae-hee breathes softly]

51
03:27.187 --> 03:29.565
[mutters] Oh, you little punk, I mean, seriously.

52
03:29.648 --> 03:30.566
[grunts]

53
03:32.151 --> 03:34.194
[breathes deeply]

54
03:34.903 --> 03:35.904
[Yi-jun clears throat]

55
03:36.280 --> 03:37.114
[inhales]

56
03:38.282 --> 03:41.452
Special Forces, uh, it's time to wake up now.

57
03:41.910 --> 03:45.289
There's an urgent work matter that I need to discuss with you.

58
03:45.372 --> 03:46.957
[groaning]

59
03:48.876 --> 03:51.295
[Yi-jun breathes deeply]

60
03:52.588 --> 03:53.630
Special Forces.

61
03:54.965 --> 03:56.008
Hey, Special Forces.

62
03:56.091 --> 03:57.217
Come on, wake up.

63
03:57.801 --> 03:58.802
You wanna get fired, huh?

64
03:59.970 --> 04:01.722
[twinkling effect]

65
04:04.183 --> 04:05.851
[dreamy music playing]

66
04:05.934 --> 04:07.895
[Jae-hee shushing]

67
04:07.978 --> 04:10.606
[heart pounding]

68
04:10.689 --> 04:12.232
[flustered exhale]

69
04:12.316 --> 04:14.359
-So loud… -[gasps]

70
04:17.613 --> 04:20.115
[soft gasping]

71
04:22.951 --> 04:24.078
[breathes softly]

72
04:24.161 --> 04:26.288
[heart pounding]

73
04:28.999 --> 04:30.167
[soft gasp]

74
04:30.834 --> 04:34.505
[soft gasping]

75
04:34.588 --> 04:35.923
[record screeching effect]

76
04:36.840 --> 04:39.259
[gentle playful music playing]

77
04:46.934 --> 04:47.768
Hey.

78
04:51.063 --> 04:52.564
It's time to wake up, okay?

79
04:54.191 --> 04:55.192
Huh?

80
04:56.860 --> 04:57.820
What?

81
04:59.113 --> 05:00.280
Shh.

82
05:00.364 --> 05:01.198
[gasps]

83
05:01.824 --> 05:02.866
[blows air]

84
05:02.950 --> 05:04.284
-[heart pounding] -[gasps]

85
05:06.537 --> 05:07.871
[grunts, whimpers]

86
05:13.252 --> 05:17.047
[soft groaning]

87
05:17.131 --> 05:20.551
[breathing deeply]

88
05:21.927 --> 05:24.805
LOVE IN DISGUISE

89
05:26.723 --> 05:28.433
[birds chirping]

90
05:28.517 --> 05:30.602
EPISODE 5

91
05:35.149 --> 05:36.650
[groaning]

92
05:39.528 --> 05:40.696
[inhales]

93
05:43.824 --> 05:44.658
Hmm?

94
05:46.702 --> 05:47.619
[groans]

95
05:50.414 --> 05:51.248
Hmm?

96
05:53.792 --> 05:54.710
[gasps]

97
05:54.793 --> 05:56.837
Whoa! Oh, uh…

98
05:56.920 --> 05:57.880
What the heck?

99
05:58.338 --> 05:59.298
What are you doing here?

100
05:59.381 --> 06:00.465
This is my house.

101
06:00.549 --> 06:01.383
Huh?

102
06:02.259 --> 06:03.302
Oh…

103
06:03.385 --> 06:04.845
Well, it is your house.

104
06:06.388 --> 06:09.308
What am I doing in your house?

105
06:09.391 --> 06:11.393
[breathes sharply]

106
06:11.476 --> 06:12.436
[awkward chuckle]

107
06:12.519 --> 06:15.439
I guess… you really don't remember.

108
06:16.106 --> 06:17.399
[soft sigh]

109
06:17.482 --> 06:20.277
You're in deep trouble if that's really the case.

110
06:22.029 --> 06:23.030
Yeah…

111
06:23.113 --> 06:25.157
[sucks teeth, groans]

112
06:25.240 --> 06:27.910
[playful jazz music playing]

113
06:28.994 --> 06:29.828
[gasps]

114
06:29.912 --> 06:31.872
Oh, what the… Whose clothes are these?

115
06:31.955 --> 06:33.665
[gasps] What's all this?

116
06:33.749 --> 06:34.833
-Wh-what is-- -[yelps]

117
06:34.917 --> 06:35.792
Whoa!

118
06:36.543 --> 06:37.377
-Oh, no! -[grunts]

119
06:37.461 --> 06:38.462
Let me apologize.

120
06:38.921 --> 06:41.298
I'm so sorry, sir. [cries]

121
06:41.381 --> 06:42.382
[breathes shakily]

122
06:43.258 --> 06:46.553
-[engine revving] -[tires screeching]

123
06:52.142 --> 06:53.560
[tires screeching]

124
06:55.812 --> 06:58.232
[soft quirky music playing]

125
07:06.740 --> 07:08.033
Um, hang on, sir.

126
07:09.451 --> 07:10.953
I remember what happened.

127
07:11.536 --> 07:12.704
-Really? -Yeah.

128
07:12.788 --> 07:13.747
Then why don't you tell me?

129
07:14.331 --> 07:16.541
First, although I told you it wasn't necessary,

130
07:16.625 --> 07:19.836
you insisted on taking me to that room on the second floor again.

131
07:20.462 --> 07:21.380
And?

132
07:22.214 --> 07:23.632
And… [gasps]

133
07:23.715 --> 07:27.803
…that's when I officially apologized for mistaking you for a perverted otaku.

134
07:29.054 --> 07:29.888
And?

135
07:31.181 --> 07:33.725
And… Ah! The type of girl you're into.

136
07:37.145 --> 07:38.480
I got a good look at her.

137
07:38.563 --> 07:39.439
-Yeah. -Yeah.

138
07:39.940 --> 07:41.191
[inhales]

139
07:41.942 --> 07:43.026
And?

140
07:44.653 --> 07:45.487
And?

141
07:47.739 --> 07:49.491
There's something else?

142
07:51.034 --> 07:52.035
[soft scoff]

143
07:52.828 --> 07:54.037
You don't remember.

144
07:54.663 --> 07:56.164
-[sighs] -It's pretty clear that you don't.

145
07:56.248 --> 07:58.500
There's no apology that could make up for it.

146
07:58.583 --> 08:00.168
Did I make a terrible mistake?

147
08:00.752 --> 08:01.753
A "mistake"?

148
08:01.837 --> 08:05.716
What you did kept me up the whole night, but you don't even remember doing it.

149
08:05.799 --> 08:08.093
Oh, you were up the whole night because of me?

150
08:08.176 --> 08:09.636
-I was not. -Huh?

151
08:09.720 --> 08:11.888
[tuts, breathes sharply]

152
08:11.972 --> 08:13.640
Fine. I was up all night.

153
08:13.724 --> 08:16.101
Although… I wasn't up all night because of you.

154
08:16.184 --> 08:17.477
[woman] Oppa!

155
08:18.770 --> 08:20.689
You were up the whole night?

156
08:20.772 --> 08:23.483
[quirky music playing]

157
08:23.567 --> 08:25.402
[dramatic music sting]

158
08:26.737 --> 08:27.904
It's been a while.

159
08:29.740 --> 08:31.116
Fiancé.

160
08:38.290 --> 08:39.624
[sighs]

161
08:42.044 --> 08:44.755
[Jae-hee] Captain, I figured it out.

162
08:45.380 --> 08:46.715
-Yoon Yi-jun… -[Captain Park sighs]

163
08:46.798 --> 08:48.050
I don't like it.

164
08:51.345 --> 08:52.596
She couldn't have…

165
08:54.139 --> 08:55.474
[Seok-jin sighs]

166
08:55.557 --> 08:57.976
[groaning]

167
08:58.477 --> 08:59.561
Do you think

168
08:59.644 --> 09:02.522
she's sending us some kind of signal, like a secret message?

169
09:03.315 --> 09:05.400
You know, like an anagram or Morse code.

170
09:05.901 --> 09:07.736
-[Captain Park sighs] -"Captain, I figured it out.

171
09:07.819 --> 09:09.654
Yoon Yi-jun is into something."

172
09:09.738 --> 09:11.865
"Dit dit dit." Ugh, seriously.

173
09:11.948 --> 09:13.950
How is this text Morse code, you lunkhead?

174
09:14.034 --> 09:16.244
No, she got hammered, and she sent us a drunk text.

175
09:17.037 --> 09:18.330
Yeah, that tracks.

176
09:18.413 --> 09:20.165
She got hammered and drunk-texted us.

177
09:20.248 --> 09:22.292
How could she drink after promising us not to?

178
09:22.376 --> 09:23.919
She knows what happens when she gets drunk.

179
09:24.002 --> 09:25.879
How could she do this to us? Jeez!

180
09:25.962 --> 09:27.130
Hey, don't take it out on me.

181
09:27.214 --> 09:28.048
I wasn't drunk.

182
09:28.131 --> 09:28.965
All right, that's it.

183
09:29.049 --> 09:30.467
I need to keep you on a tight leash.

184
09:30.550 --> 09:31.843
-Honestly, I ought to just-- -[bangs on table]

185
09:32.928 --> 09:33.845
[Seok-jin] Listen up.

186
09:33.929 --> 09:35.555
Yoon Yi-jun's fiancée is in town.

187
09:36.014 --> 09:38.016
-The Naon Art Center director? -Yeah.

188
09:38.934 --> 09:41.728
Her grandfather formerly served as the Minister of Justice.

189
09:41.812 --> 09:43.313
Pop's gonna run for president.

190
09:43.397 --> 09:44.231
She's untouchable.

191
09:44.314 --> 09:45.315
What? Really?

192
09:45.857 --> 09:46.691
Yeah, he's right.

193
09:47.359 --> 09:48.819
See? You should listen to me.

194
09:50.237 --> 09:51.196
Also…

195
09:52.114 --> 09:53.740
there's something else that I heard.

196
09:54.825 --> 09:55.951
What?

197
09:56.034 --> 09:58.912
Well, I heard… she's kind of a nutcase.

198
10:01.456 --> 10:04.918
[playful music playing]

199
10:06.753 --> 10:07.838
Bonjour.

200
10:07.921 --> 10:09.256
[flustered gasp]

201
10:09.339 --> 10:10.382
Hello there.

202
10:10.882 --> 10:12.884
Uh… it's nice to meet you.

203
10:13.552 --> 10:16.138
Stop messing with my secretary and take a seat.

204
10:18.432 --> 10:20.767
You were in Paris. When did you get back?

205
10:20.851 --> 10:21.935
[woman] Hmm…

206
10:22.018 --> 10:24.396
I came back because I missed you.

207
10:24.479 --> 10:25.856
Oh, come on, don't gross me out.

208
10:25.939 --> 10:28.608
[giggles] So cute.

209
10:29.192 --> 10:32.195
You're the cutest when you look disgusted.

210
10:33.071 --> 10:34.114
Did you have sex?

211
10:34.197 --> 10:35.449
-[gasps] No, ma'am! -We did not!

212
10:38.076 --> 10:39.453
Hmm… too bad.

213
10:39.536 --> 10:41.621
That would've been a nice hit for my dopamine levels.

214
10:41.705 --> 10:42.956
-It's not like that. -It's not like that.

215
10:45.459 --> 10:47.127
Then why are you in your pajamas,

216
10:47.210 --> 10:50.755
and why is the secretary wearing your clothes around the house?

217
10:51.590 --> 10:53.091
-It's not what you think. -Uh…

218
10:54.426 --> 10:55.427
Just leave it.

219
10:57.429 --> 10:58.263
All right then.

220
10:58.847 --> 11:00.515
I'll play along and pretend nothing happened.

221
11:00.599 --> 11:02.100
-'Cause it didn't! -Nothing happened between us!

222
11:02.517 --> 11:03.351
-Uh… -You…

223
11:03.435 --> 11:04.269
-Why won't… -Let me…

224
11:04.352 --> 11:05.187
-…you let… -…get a word in…

225
11:05.270 --> 11:06.438
-Just shh! -I mean…

226
11:08.732 --> 11:10.066
Get ready for work and come back.

227
11:11.526 --> 11:12.527
[sighs]

228
11:16.072 --> 11:17.115
[soft giggle]

229
11:18.867 --> 11:19.826
[frustrated sigh]

230
11:21.077 --> 11:21.912
Fine.

231
11:22.412 --> 11:24.164
You want me gone now that she's here, huh?

232
11:34.841 --> 11:37.010
[warbling effect]

233
11:40.430 --> 11:41.598
Ugh, I have no idea.

234
11:47.729 --> 11:50.482
Should I get jealous, or should I ignore it?

235
11:51.566 --> 11:53.401
What do you want?

236
11:54.402 --> 11:56.446
Hmm? It's just…

237
11:56.530 --> 11:58.490
in the shows I watch, people have flings with, date,

238
11:58.573 --> 12:00.659
or even cheat on their spouses with their secretaries.

239
12:00.742 --> 12:02.244
Except he's a guy.

240
12:02.327 --> 12:04.079
So what?

241
12:05.330 --> 12:08.166
I guess the jet lag is making your brain a little bit soft.

242
12:08.542 --> 12:10.502
Stop talking nonsense and go to bed.

243
12:10.585 --> 12:12.462
Mm… now that was harsh.

244
12:12.546 --> 12:14.506
You'd kick me out, but you'd let him sleep here?

245
12:16.007 --> 12:18.343
Now you're really going to make me jealous.

246
12:18.426 --> 12:20.178
Leave, I'm tired.

247
12:20.262 --> 12:22.639
-[claps] -Oh, so about the shopping bags I brought…

248
12:22.722 --> 12:23.848
Leave them.

249
12:24.724 --> 12:26.851
They're mine. Why would I leave them here?

250
12:27.477 --> 12:30.647
Hmm? I just bought a few odds and ends, nothing too fancy.

251
12:32.774 --> 12:33.733
Process these for me.

252
12:33.817 --> 12:34.693
Why should I do that?

253
12:34.776 --> 12:36.319
I turned the security cameras off

254
12:36.403 --> 12:38.196
and made sure the hallway was empty for you.

255
12:39.614 --> 12:42.075
I gave you a discount since we're so close.

256
12:42.576 --> 12:43.493
[sighs]

257
12:44.119 --> 12:45.495
All right, just go.

258
12:45.579 --> 12:46.997
By the way,

259
12:47.497 --> 12:49.541
do you drink more these days?

260
12:50.375 --> 12:51.793
Or was it just a long night?

261
12:53.712 --> 12:56.381
Somehow you seem all flustered this morning.

262
12:56.464 --> 12:59.217
Is it because your heart… skipped a beat?

263
12:59.718 --> 13:00.552
Is that why?

264
13:07.851 --> 13:09.185
[groans]

265
13:09.269 --> 13:10.812
I don't remember.

266
13:12.063 --> 13:15.400
[sighs] Kang Jae-hee, what the hell did you do last night?

267
13:18.445 --> 13:20.030
All right, let me think a second.

268
13:20.572 --> 13:23.158
Of all the crazy things you could be into.

269
13:23.241 --> 13:24.534
[inhales, blows air]

270
13:24.618 --> 13:26.661
You're dorky for collecting them.

271
13:26.745 --> 13:28.705
Pervert. You otaku.

272
13:29.164 --> 13:30.206
I drank alcohol.

273
13:30.290 --> 13:32.917
-You little munchkin! -[Jerry yowling]

274
13:33.001 --> 13:34.044
[strained grunt]

275
13:34.502 --> 13:35.670
Then I caught the cat.

276
13:40.717 --> 13:41.801
It's all gone.

277
13:41.885 --> 13:44.304
[frustrated grunting]

278
13:44.387 --> 13:45.889
[panting]

279
13:45.972 --> 13:46.806
I will not!

280
13:46.890 --> 13:47.974
[yells] Hey!

281
13:48.725 --> 13:49.684
Joking!

282
13:50.268 --> 13:51.811
Oh, my brain hurts.

283
13:52.896 --> 13:53.730
[sighs]

284
14:00.487 --> 14:02.572
[breathes deeply]

285
14:03.865 --> 14:05.033
"Skipped a beat"?

286
14:06.618 --> 14:07.827
"Flustered"?

287
14:07.911 --> 14:09.913
It was 'cause I was feeling disgusted

288
14:10.455 --> 14:12.123
by my secretary's mistake.

289
14:16.294 --> 14:18.463
[Yi-jun sighs] It doesn't make sense.

290
14:18.546 --> 14:20.465
How could he not remember any of it?

291
14:28.598 --> 14:29.474
[sighs]

292
14:30.684 --> 14:32.102
I need to get it together.

293
14:35.438 --> 14:36.398
[sighs]

294
14:38.316 --> 14:40.318
[breathes deeply]

295
14:42.987 --> 14:44.614
MOBILE CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION TEAM 1 CAPT, I FIGGEDITOUT, YUNIJN…

296
14:44.698 --> 14:45.865
WAN-GU: ?? BONG-YI: KANG JAE-HEE? WHAT HAPPENED?

297
14:45.949 --> 14:46.908
BONG-YI HYUNG

298
14:46.991 --> 14:48.493
-[phone buzzing] -[gasps]

299
14:50.954 --> 14:52.747
What do I do? [sighs]

300
14:53.665 --> 14:54.541
Salute.

301
14:55.166 --> 14:56.042
Yeah, all right.

302
14:56.126 --> 14:57.043
Salute you back.

303
14:57.127 --> 14:59.504
Despite all that talk about a superior's orders

304
14:59.587 --> 15:01.506
being a matter of life and death,

305
15:01.589 --> 15:04.592
you seem to have had no qualms about completely ignoring my orders last night.

306
15:05.051 --> 15:06.928
Well, I mean, uh, the deed is done.

307
15:07.011 --> 15:08.138
What can we do about it?

308
15:08.221 --> 15:09.973
What's that? "What can we do about it?"

309
15:10.056 --> 15:12.684
Oh, come on, that is some horseshit! Seriously!

310
15:12.767 --> 15:15.687
Besides, sir, I didn't screw up last night.

311
15:16.396 --> 15:17.939
I just did what I usually do.

312
15:18.898 --> 15:21.901
I just kinda… ran around.

313
15:21.985 --> 15:24.612
[Jae-hee] Anything you say can be used against you.

314
15:24.696 --> 15:25.780
Where are my handcuffs?

315
15:28.783 --> 15:30.660
You must be crazy.

316
15:30.744 --> 15:32.203
You must be crazy!

317
15:32.287 --> 15:33.705
What was that?

318
15:33.788 --> 15:35.081
Did you just call me crazy?

319
15:35.165 --> 15:37.667
Why, you little punk, a-are you just ignoring rank now or what?

320
15:38.793 --> 15:40.587
What do you mean, I'm ignoring rank?

321
15:40.670 --> 15:43.923
I would have to be an insane person if I went up against you, sir.

322
15:44.382 --> 15:46.843
The alcohol I drank was a means to an end.

323
15:46.926 --> 15:49.220
And while sacrificing myself, I figured it out.

324
15:49.304 --> 15:50.805
[laughs] Sa--

325
15:50.889 --> 15:51.931
Oh, really?

326
15:52.015 --> 15:52.849
[scoffs]

327
15:52.932 --> 15:55.685
Okay then, let's hear what you found out through this self-sacrifice.

328
15:56.186 --> 15:58.980
Yoon Yi-jun… shouldn't be considered a suspect.

329
15:59.063 --> 16:00.565
He said he didn't do it.

330
16:00.648 --> 16:02.525
If anything, he's racked with guilt over her death.

331
16:02.609 --> 16:03.902
Hey, what do you mean?

332
16:03.985 --> 16:05.028
Are you sure?

333
16:06.613 --> 16:08.865
Yoon Yi-jun said this himself, huh?

334
16:08.948 --> 16:09.824
Yeah.

335
16:10.325 --> 16:11.701
I think he's being sincere.

336
16:12.535 --> 16:13.495
Which means…

337
16:14.412 --> 16:16.331
the real killer is still out there.

338
16:16.956 --> 16:20.251
The chandelier, the herbicide… I think they're targeting Yoon Yi-jun.

339
16:20.877 --> 16:22.378
[superior] Where are those pricks?

340
16:25.256 --> 16:26.966
-Oh… -[quirky music playing]

341
16:27.050 --> 16:28.802
Where the hell is Captain Park?

342
16:30.220 --> 16:32.555
[groaning]

343
16:32.639 --> 16:34.182
He's looking for you.

344
16:37.894 --> 16:38.895
[inhales]

345
16:39.437 --> 16:40.522
[sighs]

346
16:41.231 --> 16:42.273
Come outside.

347
16:43.066 --> 16:44.692
Outside, now.

348
16:46.820 --> 16:47.654
Your phone, sir.

349
16:50.323 --> 16:51.407
[Wan-gu] Dude, look out.

350
16:51.991 --> 16:53.743
-Warned you. -[Captain Park groans]

351
16:59.415 --> 17:00.667
Will the captain be okay?

352
17:01.543 --> 17:04.921
Maybe I should've gone with him to say, "Yoon Yi-jun's being threatened.

353
17:05.004 --> 17:07.173
It looks like someone else killed Ms. Han."

354
17:07.257 --> 17:08.466
Should I say that, head held high?

355
17:08.550 --> 17:11.010
Why don't you tell him about our undercover investigation too?

356
17:11.094 --> 17:13.096
This drives me nuts, it really does.

357
17:13.721 --> 17:14.639
[sighs]

358
17:15.306 --> 17:17.475
Guess I should continue my undercover work.

359
17:18.142 --> 17:19.435
I'll look into the herbicide.

360
17:19.519 --> 17:20.895
Detective Kang may be onto something.

361
17:20.979 --> 17:22.021
Okay.

362
17:22.814 --> 17:23.648
Hey.

363
17:24.524 --> 17:26.526
The captain's gonna be fine, right?

364
17:26.609 --> 17:28.194
CHIEF'S OFFICE

365
17:28.278 --> 17:29.362
[Captain Park] A ph-phone?

366
17:29.946 --> 17:33.032
Uh, I'm not… not quite sure what phone you're talking about.

367
17:33.658 --> 17:35.285
[tense music sting]

368
17:38.413 --> 17:41.082
Well, I heard of it while going through the settlement with the family.

369
17:41.583 --> 17:43.042
They said they notified you.

370
17:43.126 --> 17:46.629
Ms. Han Eun-young had two phones, did she not?

371
17:48.047 --> 17:49.048
Why didn't you tell me?

372
17:50.133 --> 17:52.260
Well, I only found out about this just recently, sir.

373
17:53.511 --> 17:55.889
So are you actively looking for it or not?

374
17:56.264 --> 17:59.475
Well, um, we think it must have gone missing from the scene.

375
18:00.101 --> 18:01.978
-Uh… -[superior] Are you sure it wasn't there?

376
18:02.061 --> 18:03.187
What was on it?

377
18:04.355 --> 18:06.691
That's something I'd also like to know, sir.

378
18:06.774 --> 18:07.859
But, uh…

379
18:07.942 --> 18:09.944
Well, I can't exactly request a warrant

380
18:10.028 --> 18:11.905
to search Taekang headquarters, so…

381
18:11.988 --> 18:12.989
-Uh, you… -Uh, yeah.

382
18:13.072 --> 18:14.282
So that's the current situation.

383
18:14.365 --> 18:15.575
Detective…

384
18:17.243 --> 18:20.038
where do you think that phone is now? Hmm?

385
18:21.122 --> 18:23.625
-[tense music playing] -[camera shutter clicking]

386
18:23.708 --> 18:24.792
[camera whirs]

387
18:28.254 --> 18:29.631
I'll leave it to you.

388
18:29.714 --> 18:30.798
Take care, ma'am.

389
18:34.177 --> 18:35.511
[car door opens]

390
18:36.304 --> 18:37.555
[camera shutter clicking]

391
18:37.639 --> 18:40.725
Yoon Na-jung met Kim Si-hyun as soon as Chairman Yoon

392
18:40.808 --> 18:42.518
called off the succession.

393
18:43.227 --> 18:45.313
[Captain Park] Strange timing, if you ask me.

394
18:47.565 --> 18:49.984
Well, uh, the phone, you know, the victim… [chuckles]

395
18:50.068 --> 18:52.779
…they might have lost it somewhere. [chuckles]

396
18:52.862 --> 18:54.030
I guess…

397
18:55.698 --> 18:56.532
you'd have it…

398
18:57.492 --> 18:58.993
if you knew where it was, no?

399
18:59.077 --> 19:00.286
Of course we would.

400
19:00.370 --> 19:02.830
[superior chuckles] Besides, it might not even exist.

401
19:02.914 --> 19:05.375
Could be something the family made up.

402
19:05.458 --> 19:06.834
Can't hurt to be careful.

403
19:07.335 --> 19:09.212
Please recover it as soon as you can.

404
19:09.587 --> 19:12.256
As always, Taekang will help however we can

405
19:12.340 --> 19:13.716
should you require any assistance.

406
19:13.800 --> 19:15.093
Right. Thank you.

407
19:15.593 --> 19:18.513
Rest assured, this investigation will be handled by the book.

408
19:18.596 --> 19:19.681
By the way, Detective Park,

409
19:20.390 --> 19:22.684
your team is just the detectives we met before, right?

410
19:23.101 --> 19:23.977
That's your whole team?

411
19:25.353 --> 19:26.813
I don't know if it's 'cause you're a lawyer,

412
19:26.896 --> 19:27.939
but you have a great memory.

413
19:28.022 --> 19:30.733
His team's those guys you met before and one more idiot.

414
19:30.817 --> 19:32.902
That's it. There's just four of them.

415
19:32.986 --> 19:36.781
Man, people make such a huge fuss about sexual discrimination these days,

416
19:36.864 --> 19:39.200
but the female detective on the team causes more trouble

417
19:39.283 --> 19:41.035
than a man ever could.

418
19:42.412 --> 19:44.497
A female detective?

419
19:44.580 --> 19:48.376
By the way, uh, I'm guessing you're q-quite popular with the ladies,

420
19:48.459 --> 19:50.169
given how handsome you are, right? Right?

421
19:50.253 --> 19:51.838
I mean, if you're a big shot lawyer,

422
19:51.921 --> 19:54.048
I bet you got a line of ladies, huh?

423
19:54.132 --> 19:56.009
Not like this guy. He was unpopular.

424
19:56.092 --> 19:57.093
He joined the force a year after me.

425
19:57.176 --> 19:58.386
Wow.

426
19:58.469 --> 19:59.512
Isn't he handsome?

427
19:59.595 --> 20:01.514
[door bell jingles]

428
20:10.606 --> 20:11.482
[exhales]

429
20:12.233 --> 20:13.151
Oh, I needed that.

430
20:13.234 --> 20:14.944
[phone buzzing]

431
20:16.446 --> 20:17.447
[soft gasp]

432
20:20.616 --> 20:21.451
Sir.

433
20:21.951 --> 20:22.785
Where are you?

434
20:23.369 --> 20:25.079
Have you decided to quit before you get fired?

435
20:25.830 --> 20:26.831
I'm on my way.

436
20:26.914 --> 20:28.624
I need you here in ten minutes.

437
20:28.708 --> 20:29.792
Is that clear?

438
20:29.876 --> 20:30.877
Oh, I think I might need

439
20:30.960 --> 20:33.046
-a little more than-- Hello? -[line disconnects]

440
20:35.506 --> 20:36.466
[sighs]

441
20:37.175 --> 20:38.509
Ah, think, think.

442
20:39.385 --> 20:40.219
Okay.

443
20:42.138 --> 20:43.723
If he figured out that I was a cop,

444
20:44.432 --> 20:47.393
he probably would've thrown a fit and had Kim Si-hyun sue me.

445
20:48.644 --> 20:51.230
Or… if he'd figured out I was a woman,

446
20:51.314 --> 20:54.400
he'd just have Kim Si-hyun fire me on the spot, given his temper.

447
20:55.068 --> 20:55.902
[sucks teeth]

448
20:55.985 --> 20:58.821
In that case, it seems he's just being crabby as usual.

449
21:02.033 --> 21:03.659
Maybe I didn't mess up that bad.

450
21:03.743 --> 21:05.870
I guess you really don't remember.

451
21:05.953 --> 21:08.664
You're in deep trouble if that's really the case.

452
21:08.748 --> 21:11.292
[frustrated groan] Oh, I am in deep trouble!

453
21:11.375 --> 21:12.293
This is bad!

454
21:14.170 --> 21:15.379
Should I run for it?

455
21:15.463 --> 21:16.380
Yeah, let's do it!

456
21:23.179 --> 21:24.639
[nervous sigh]

457
21:24.722 --> 21:26.182
-[door opens] -[sucks teeth]

458
21:28.476 --> 21:29.477
[door closes]

459
21:39.779 --> 21:40.696
Sorry, sir.

460
21:42.031 --> 21:43.908
-So, last night, uh-- -[Yi-jun] You have two options.

461
21:43.991 --> 21:45.910
I might get Kim Si-hyun to sue you,

462
21:46.577 --> 21:48.204
or I'll get him to ax you.

463
21:50.248 --> 21:52.917
I'm still deciding, so behave yourself and wait.

464
21:56.921 --> 21:57.880
[Jae-hee] Ta-da!

465
21:58.965 --> 22:01.050
I picked this up for you on my way here, sir,

466
22:01.134 --> 22:02.885
in case your stomach was hurting.

467
22:03.427 --> 22:05.388
[tuts] Ah…

468
22:05.930 --> 22:08.182
My personal secretary has thoughtfully brought me

469
22:08.266 --> 22:10.852
a Taekang competitor's product, has he?

470
22:12.186 --> 22:14.063
Oh, yeah, well, um…

471
22:16.232 --> 22:19.735
And this bottle is a one-plus-one prepackaged set of two.

472
22:19.819 --> 22:21.154
You have it wrong.

473
22:21.237 --> 22:22.780
That wasn't my intention at all, sir.

474
22:22.864 --> 22:25.032
You bought it for your upset stomach, didn't you?

475
22:25.116 --> 22:26.826
So you can just quit the nice guy act.

476
22:26.909 --> 22:27.743
Not at all.

477
22:27.827 --> 22:30.621
I was worried your stomach might be just as upset as my stomach,

478
22:30.705 --> 22:33.124
so I only drank one, although I could have taken both.

479
22:33.207 --> 22:34.250
That's why I got this.

480
22:34.792 --> 22:36.210
Paid for with my own money.

481
22:36.669 --> 22:38.337
Don't you think this goes to show you, sir,

482
22:38.421 --> 22:40.298
that I really do care for you?

483
22:45.178 --> 22:46.846
You don't remember what happened,

484
22:46.929 --> 22:48.014
but you're worried what I'm thinking,

485
22:48.097 --> 22:50.975
and now you're trying to slither over the fence using cheap flattery.

486
22:51.058 --> 22:51.976
Is that it?

487
22:52.476 --> 22:53.936
What do you mean, cheap flattery?

488
22:54.020 --> 22:56.022
Come on, sir. You know how much… [inhales]

489
22:56.105 --> 22:57.815
…I care about you.

490
22:58.316 --> 22:59.442
[irritated yell]

491
22:59.525 --> 23:01.152
-Don't care so much! -Huh?

492
23:02.069 --> 23:03.404
Don't even think about me.

493
23:05.615 --> 23:06.616
Take me to work.

494
23:06.991 --> 23:07.825
You just drive.

495
23:08.743 --> 23:09.744
[sighs]

496
23:16.292 --> 23:18.920
He can't be that mad if he took the drink, though, right?

497
23:30.765 --> 23:31.766
[Yi-jun sighs softly]

498
23:31.849 --> 23:32.725
Out with it.

499
23:32.808 --> 23:33.684
Out with what?

500
23:39.774 --> 23:41.525
Uh, about last night…

501
23:45.321 --> 23:46.739
Uh, has Ms. Lee left yet?

502
23:47.490 --> 23:48.991
[inhales] Ms. Lee?

503
23:49.533 --> 23:50.868
Why do you care if she's still there?

504
23:51.494 --> 23:54.872
Oh, she… was so beautiful. That's all.

505
23:57.541 --> 23:58.876
Special Forces…

506
23:58.960 --> 24:00.253
you're more ambitious than I thought.

507
24:00.336 --> 24:01.379
Sir?

508
24:01.462 --> 24:04.590
Well, Lee Si-a has a lot to offer, I guess.

509
24:04.674 --> 24:07.385
Makes sense… you'd find her interesting.

510
24:07.468 --> 24:08.552
Whoa, what are you talking about?

511
24:08.636 --> 24:11.180
I… I was only asking because the two of you look so great together.

512
24:11.264 --> 24:12.181
Although…

513
24:12.682 --> 24:15.184
you are, of course, too good for her. [chuckles]

514
24:15.768 --> 24:16.727
What?

515
24:16.811 --> 24:19.313
You're exceptionally good-looking, highly capable,

516
24:19.397 --> 24:20.815
and your character is…

517
24:20.898 --> 24:22.149
[inhales]

518
24:22.233 --> 24:23.859
…so special.

519
24:23.943 --> 24:25.486
You are a rare kind of man, sir.

520
24:25.569 --> 24:27.780
[laughing]

521
24:27.863 --> 24:29.407
I get it, so just drive.

522
24:29.490 --> 24:31.075
I'm trying to work, and you're distracting.

523
24:31.867 --> 24:32.702
Yep.

524
24:34.996 --> 24:36.289
[sighs]

525
24:48.509 --> 24:50.052
You're too close. Stay back.

526
24:50.136 --> 24:51.137
Just keeping you safe.

527
24:53.681 --> 24:54.640
Five steps back.

528
24:54.724 --> 24:55.766
No, five more.

529
24:55.850 --> 24:56.726
I can't do that.

530
24:57.226 --> 24:59.645
If I'm to keep you safe, then I have to…

531
25:02.732 --> 25:06.235
[squeaking effect]

532
25:07.069 --> 25:08.446
Ten steps, right?

533
25:08.529 --> 25:09.572
Is this good enough for you, sir?

534
25:09.655 --> 25:10.823
What are you doing?

535
25:11.407 --> 25:12.241
A bit more?

536
25:13.743 --> 25:14.744
[soft chuckle]

537
25:16.078 --> 25:16.912
This much?

538
25:17.496 --> 25:18.414
You're cute.

539
25:18.789 --> 25:19.790
Whoa, hell no!

540
25:19.874 --> 25:21.083
-Yes, sir! -[squeaking effect]

541
25:21.792 --> 25:22.877
[soft gasp]

542
25:25.921 --> 25:27.089
[groans]

543
25:27.173 --> 25:28.591
Uh… Um, sir?

544
25:29.175 --> 25:30.051
Wait, sir!

545
25:32.094 --> 25:34.388
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

546
25:36.640 --> 25:38.893
I heard Mr. Yoon came into work today.

547
25:40.853 --> 25:43.731
Even I was surprised that you canceled the share transfer, sir.

548
25:43.814 --> 25:47.318
I plan on checking in on them and seeing what they're up to.

549
25:47.651 --> 25:48.652
Sir?

550
25:51.906 --> 25:54.533
Why bother dropping my cubs off a cliff

551
25:54.617 --> 25:56.077
when the strongest one

552
25:56.160 --> 25:58.704
will claim the meat for itself if I leave them be?

553
26:01.040 --> 26:01.916
Isn't that right?

554
26:05.086 --> 26:06.587
I heard that Ms. Lee

555
26:06.670 --> 26:08.756
went to see Mr. Yoon as soon as she arrived in town.

556
26:09.799 --> 26:11.425
I'll have to meet up with her father.

557
26:12.551 --> 26:14.011
I'll set up an appointment.

558
26:14.095 --> 26:15.346
With the polls coming up,

559
26:15.429 --> 26:17.723
we would want their wedding to occur before the election.

560
26:17.807 --> 26:19.141
Of course.

561
26:28.526 --> 26:29.443
[door opens]

562
26:33.155 --> 26:34.240
[engine stops]

563
26:36.367 --> 26:37.368
Hmm…

564
26:39.453 --> 26:42.164
So the police are looking for the phone, are they?

565
26:49.630 --> 26:50.798
TAESPATCH

566
26:50.881 --> 26:54.135
Ms. Lee, do you need someone to go to the TF team to run an errand?

567
26:54.552 --> 26:55.469
I'll volunteer for that.

568
26:55.553 --> 26:56.429
[soft chuckle]

569
26:56.512 --> 26:57.596
You wanna see Mr. Kang?

570
26:57.680 --> 26:58.681
Totally.

571
26:58.764 --> 26:59.807
He's so my type.

572
27:00.474 --> 27:02.810
It'd be nice if I could run into him in the cafeteria.

573
27:02.893 --> 27:04.979
-[secretary] Oh. -[footsteps approaching]

574
27:05.062 --> 27:06.814
I'd like an iced milk tea, please.

575
27:16.907 --> 27:18.200
[dramatic music sting]

576
27:18.284 --> 27:21.662
[tense music playing]

577
27:24.707 --> 27:26.208
[elevator dings]

578
27:40.764 --> 27:42.475
Yeah, thanks for handling that for me.

579
27:42.558 --> 27:44.059
I'm glad I could help out.

580
27:44.143 --> 27:47.188
You can just call. I'm just around.

581
28:04.455 --> 28:06.081
[phone buzzing]

582
28:11.462 --> 28:13.714
[Captain Park] You know Kim Si-hyun knows about the missing phone, right?

583
28:13.797 --> 28:15.549
Ah, it just rubs me the wrong way.

584
28:15.633 --> 28:17.510
He's acting way too suspiciously.

585
28:17.593 --> 28:18.844
He's involved in everything.

586
28:18.928 --> 28:22.139
He's a sharp son of a bitch, so he'll assume we're looking for it.

587
28:22.223 --> 28:24.683
We need to be quick. We have to find that phone first.

588
28:24.767 --> 28:26.602
I've looked through every place she could have gone.

589
28:26.685 --> 28:28.020
The phone's not here. It's just not.

590
28:28.729 --> 28:29.939
Look, if you ask me,

591
28:30.022 --> 28:32.525
there's a better chance the phone's at Yoon Yi-jun's house.

592
28:32.608 --> 28:34.652
Of course it's there. You just suck at looking for it.

593
28:34.735 --> 28:36.820
Hey, if that's the best you can do, maybe you should quit.

594
28:36.904 --> 28:38.948
[Captain Park] What have you been doing there anyway, huh?

595
28:39.031 --> 28:40.741
What have you accomplished while you've been there

596
28:40.824 --> 28:41.825
aside from getting a rash?

597
28:41.909 --> 28:44.745
Just 'cause Kim Si-hyun outplayed you doesn't mean you can take it out on me.

598
28:44.828 --> 28:45.704
I'm not your punching bag.

599
28:45.788 --> 28:47.206
What did you say? What?

600
28:47.289 --> 28:48.457
[Wan-gu] Uh, just hang on.

601
28:48.541 --> 28:49.583
There's one more place.

602
28:50.334 --> 28:52.336
EQUIPMENT STORAGE

603
28:52.962 --> 28:54.296
I'll have to pick a lock.

604
28:55.714 --> 29:01.345
6 DAYS AGO

605
29:01.428 --> 29:02.888
[Young-sook] Well, well.

606
29:03.806 --> 29:05.432
You said you'd come and help me out,

607
29:05.516 --> 29:08.060
but I see you're just wasting time, aren't you?

608
29:08.686 --> 29:10.271
You don't need to clean that one. It's new.

609
29:10.813 --> 29:12.898
No one sits there, so they switched the old desk out.

610
29:13.607 --> 29:15.818
-[drawer slides close] -They switched out the old desk?

611
29:15.901 --> 29:18.654
Haven't you heard? What happened to the girl that sat there?

612
29:18.737 --> 29:19.572
Oh, yes.

613
29:19.655 --> 29:20.906
Seems a bit odd, though.

614
29:21.490 --> 29:23.075
Why would they switch out the desk?

615
29:23.158 --> 29:24.451
Well…

616
29:24.535 --> 29:27.246
I guess they're looking out for whoever's gonna take that spot.

617
29:27.746 --> 29:29.915
Ugh, no one even sits there right now,

618
29:29.999 --> 29:33.002
so I don't know who the hell asked to get this desk swapped out anyway.

619
29:33.502 --> 29:36.922
Well, I guess you must have run into them a couple of times now and then.

620
29:37.006 --> 29:37.840
[Young-sook] Who?

621
29:38.340 --> 29:39.925
-That poor girl? -Mm-hmm.

622
29:41.260 --> 29:42.261
Oh, dear.

623
29:42.344 --> 29:44.763
Suppose all those old sayings are true.

624
29:45.723 --> 29:48.434
They say people can change when their death draws near,

625
29:48.517 --> 29:50.060
and that's exactly what happened.

626
29:50.144 --> 29:53.105
-Hmm. -I mean, something was going on.

627
29:53.188 --> 29:55.357
She was spacing out all the time, you know?

628
29:55.441 --> 29:58.027
Or she'd be talking on the phone on a call.

629
29:59.111 --> 30:00.696
[Young-sook] I overheard her once…

630
30:00.779 --> 30:03.532
Yes. I've checked over everything.

631
30:04.658 --> 30:06.660
Mr. Yoon doesn't know about it.

632
30:07.077 --> 30:09.997
[sighs] I know it's not my place to intervene…

633
30:10.623 --> 30:12.249
but things are getting much too dangerous for me--

634
30:12.333 --> 30:13.751
-[rattles] -[gasps]

635
30:13.834 --> 30:14.960
[Young-sook] But then…

636
30:19.131 --> 30:22.843
I slipped out because I felt like I shouldn't stay there any longer.

637
30:24.011 --> 30:28.098
Goodness me, and then… just a few days later,

638
30:28.599 --> 30:29.975
they found her in there.

639
30:30.059 --> 30:31.268
[sighs, tuts]

640
30:31.352 --> 30:34.313
Oh, that poor girl. Goodness…

641
30:39.943 --> 30:42.404
[keypad beeping]

642
30:44.531 --> 30:46.075
[Wan-gu] Replaced desk.

643
30:46.158 --> 30:47.409
A missing phone.

644
30:51.246 --> 30:52.831
Who was she talking to?

645
31:01.131 --> 31:03.550
-I'll be fine. Just wait outside. -[door closes]

646
31:06.845 --> 31:07.763
[sighs]

647
31:09.390 --> 31:10.391
No, wait.

648
31:11.183 --> 31:12.184
I could use some refreshment.

649
31:12.267 --> 31:13.477
Get me some milk tea.

650
31:13.560 --> 31:14.395
Yes, sir.

651
31:16.647 --> 31:18.148
[Yi-jun screams]

652
31:18.649 --> 31:20.275
[breathes angrily]

653
31:20.359 --> 31:22.027
Sir, this one's urgent.

654
31:22.111 --> 31:23.862
[yells] Are you out of your mind?

655
31:23.946 --> 31:25.572
[tense dramatic music playing]

656
31:25.656 --> 31:26.615
[breathes nervously]

657
31:30.619 --> 31:31.453
[mouths]

658
31:35.624 --> 31:37.251
[Yi-jun] My milk tea…

659
31:38.585 --> 31:40.462
[yells] Why did you add ice?

660
31:41.088 --> 31:43.048
Oh, you definitely asked for a refreshing--

661
31:43.132 --> 31:44.550
So that's how I worded it, is it?

662
31:45.259 --> 31:46.593
Listen up, Army Man.

663
31:46.677 --> 31:48.804
I'm the type of guy who gets every single word

664
31:48.887 --> 31:50.806
and detail down to the last syllable.

665
31:50.889 --> 31:51.724
[inhales]

666
31:51.807 --> 31:54.601
I need another one. [inhales]

667
31:55.436 --> 31:58.689
I expect the milk to be heated to 58 degrees.

668
31:58.772 --> 31:59.606
[yells] Again!

669
32:03.527 --> 32:05.237
-[glass clanks] -[whispers] Hurry up!

670
32:05.904 --> 32:07.030
[irritated breathing]

671
32:07.114 --> 32:10.242
So, who told you to delay my two o'clock by ten minutes?

672
32:10.325 --> 32:11.618
You told me to do that, sir.

673
32:12.703 --> 32:14.204
I'm sure that you misheard me.

674
32:14.663 --> 32:17.040
Move it up five minutes. Again!

675
32:20.335 --> 32:21.378
[breathes nervously]

676
32:22.755 --> 32:24.089
Why do you think he's being this way?

677
32:25.466 --> 32:26.717
[door closes]

678
32:26.800 --> 32:27.718
[angry grunt]

679
32:29.595 --> 32:33.307
Why does the 17-page CR report only go up to page 16?

680
32:33.974 --> 32:35.642
Is making copies that hard?

681
32:36.351 --> 32:37.269
Well, sir…

682
32:37.352 --> 32:38.812
[keyboard keys clacking]

683
32:38.896 --> 32:42.107
…you tore that page out of the report during the meeting, if you recall.

684
32:42.191 --> 32:43.400
Don't you argue with me!

685
32:44.318 --> 32:45.736
[mutters] Oh, give me a break.

686
32:46.195 --> 32:47.029
Whatever.

687
32:47.654 --> 32:50.157
-Read it. -[soft sigh]

688
32:52.284 --> 32:54.661
Wow. Wow. [soft chuckle]

689
32:55.078 --> 32:55.996
Hmm…

690
32:56.705 --> 32:58.665
"Do it again."

691
33:00.334 --> 33:01.293
"Again."

692
33:02.461 --> 33:03.629
Again!

693
33:04.546 --> 33:05.380
[sighs]

694
33:11.261 --> 33:13.263
[door opens, closes]

695
33:13.347 --> 33:15.224
I think he's doing the best he can, sir.

696
33:16.225 --> 33:18.227
I feel like you could go easier on him.

697
33:22.189 --> 33:23.565
Let me get this straight.

698
33:23.649 --> 33:26.485
You're saying that I'm being a hard-ass,

699
33:26.568 --> 33:29.321
and therefore, I'm the one in the wrong in this case?

700
33:29.738 --> 33:30.781
Yes…

701
33:31.615 --> 33:32.658
No!

702
33:33.242 --> 33:34.618
You've always been most forgiving, sir.

703
33:35.494 --> 33:37.663
Th-that Mr. Kang's the problem.

704
33:37.746 --> 33:39.331
That impertinent little, ugh…

705
33:39.414 --> 33:40.249
Right.

706
33:40.666 --> 33:43.669
I definitely tried to be forgiving and also generous to him,

707
33:43.752 --> 33:45.212
but he just had to…

708
33:45.295 --> 33:46.129
Yeah, he did.

709
33:46.213 --> 33:49.216
…continue saying all these weird things and messing with my head.

710
33:49.299 --> 33:51.134
Don't you think this goes to show you, sir,

711
33:51.218 --> 33:52.803
that I really do care for you?

712
33:52.886 --> 33:54.096
I care about you.

713
33:54.179 --> 33:56.765
You're exceptionally good-looking, highly capable,

714
33:56.849 --> 33:59.142
and your character is… [inhales]

715
33:59.852 --> 34:01.478
…so special.

716
34:01.562 --> 34:03.814
You are a rare kind of man, sir. [laughing]

717
34:05.732 --> 34:07.818
Is Mr. Kang capable of doing that, sir?

718
34:08.735 --> 34:09.653
Get out.

719
34:13.156 --> 34:15.325
-[door opens, closes] -[sighs]

720
34:15.409 --> 34:17.619
[whirring]

721
34:18.370 --> 34:20.038
Giving me the business…

722
34:20.372 --> 34:21.790
-[sighs] -[phone buzzes]

723
34:28.714 --> 34:29.715
[Wan-gu] Wee-oo, wee-oo.

724
34:40.851 --> 34:44.313
[sighs] Now what was I looking for again?

725
34:49.943 --> 34:51.486
This is a camera blind spot.

726
34:51.570 --> 34:52.946
Just keep a lookout.

727
34:53.447 --> 34:54.615
What the heck took you so long?

728
34:55.490 --> 34:58.285
Do you think a personal secretary gets paid just to hang out?

729
34:59.745 --> 35:01.288
Oh, is that it?

730
35:02.039 --> 35:04.249
Uh-huh. Fancy a guess?

731
35:04.333 --> 35:05.876
Zero-zero-zero-zero?

732
35:05.959 --> 35:07.628
Man, how easy would our job be

733
35:07.711 --> 35:09.880
if everyone in the world were as simple as you?

734
35:10.631 --> 35:11.506
One-eight-one-eight.

735
35:11.590 --> 35:13.216
Oh, hey, that's a good one. Wow.

736
35:13.300 --> 35:14.468
Have you tried it, though?

737
35:14.551 --> 35:15.636
Put it in. Give it a go.

738
35:15.719 --> 35:18.931
I actually need you to open this door, not guess the lottery winner.

739
35:19.014 --> 35:20.349
[sucks teeth] Two days.

740
35:20.432 --> 35:22.392
I'll unlock that sucker. Count on it.

741
35:24.811 --> 35:28.231
By the way, I heard Yoon Yi-jun's been a real hard-ass.

742
35:29.149 --> 35:30.651
Ah, rumors have been going around.

743
35:30.734 --> 35:32.277
Everyone feels bad for you.

744
35:32.361 --> 35:33.278
Right?

745
35:33.820 --> 35:34.821
Those rumors are true.

746
35:34.905 --> 35:36.490
I feel so bad for myself.

747
35:37.032 --> 35:38.575
I swear, he's got such a…

748
35:40.285 --> 35:41.745
shitty personality.

749
35:42.704 --> 35:43.747
So…

750
35:44.289 --> 35:46.041
the day you drunk-texted our group chat…

751
35:47.876 --> 35:49.628
you did something to Yoon Yi-jun?

752
35:53.340 --> 35:54.549
I did not.

753
35:57.135 --> 35:58.053
Cuffs?

754
35:58.136 --> 35:59.721
-[yells] Are you insane? -[bangs on table]

755
35:59.805 --> 36:01.306
[quirky music playing]

756
36:01.390 --> 36:05.811
♪ It's insane, it's insane It's insane, it's insane ♪

757
36:06.687 --> 36:07.604
Sheesh.

758
36:08.146 --> 36:09.982
Please keep it a secret from the captain.

759
36:10.065 --> 36:11.984
I'll find a way to fix it.

760
36:12.067 --> 36:12.901
[Wan-gu] I knew it.

761
36:12.985 --> 36:14.653
[sighs]

762
36:14.736 --> 36:16.571
You don't take things lying down.

763
36:17.322 --> 36:18.657
What if Yoon Yi-jun's onto you?

764
36:19.658 --> 36:20.867
No, I don't think he is.

765
36:20.951 --> 36:24.496
I don't think I'd be alive right now if he found out I was undercover.

766
36:24.579 --> 36:25.414
And our team?

767
36:25.497 --> 36:26.331
No chance.

768
36:26.873 --> 36:29.251
He'd burn our station down to the ground and fire us all.

769
36:29.334 --> 36:30.794
Ah, then why, why, why, why,

770
36:30.877 --> 36:32.462
why is he being so hard on you?

771
36:32.546 --> 36:35.340
[groans] I kinda remember running around the place

772
36:35.424 --> 36:37.175
trying to catch that damn nutty cat.

773
36:37.259 --> 36:39.553
Are you insane? [groans]

774
36:40.053 --> 36:41.596
You know what the captain's like.

775
36:41.680 --> 36:43.473
He's gonna give us hell for this crap.

776
36:43.557 --> 36:44.641
I know.

777
36:45.684 --> 36:49.479
Look, I'll buy some time until we can pick our way through that door,

778
36:49.980 --> 36:51.773
so try to remember what happened.

779
36:51.857 --> 36:52.691
-Okay? -Yeah.

780
36:52.774 --> 36:53.608
[Wan-gu sighs]

781
36:57.029 --> 36:57.946
Do you know…

782
37:00.574 --> 37:02.701
Kim Si-hyun and Yoon Na-jung met up?

783
37:03.201 --> 37:05.328
Yeah, she also tried to get me to join her.

784
37:05.412 --> 37:06.580
I think it's suspicious.

785
37:06.663 --> 37:09.708
But Kim Si-hyun, he's been friends with Yoon Yi-jun forever.

786
37:09.791 --> 37:11.585
[scoffs] So what?

787
37:11.668 --> 37:13.712
Money easily breaks friends apart.

788
37:15.172 --> 37:16.882
Besides, from what I've heard,

789
37:17.591 --> 37:19.468
they're saying Kim Si-hyun is also a rat.

790
37:19.551 --> 37:22.054
Apparently, he went scurrying to Yoon Na-jung

791
37:22.137 --> 37:25.974
and tipped her off in advance regarding the progress of the succession plans.

792
37:26.058 --> 37:27.184
[camera shutter clicking]

793
37:27.726 --> 37:31.730
Anyway, while Yoon Na-jung and Yoon Yi-jun are duking it out behind the scenes…

794
37:31.813 --> 37:32.647
-[indistinct chatter] -Sir.

795
37:32.731 --> 37:35.108
-…Chairman Yoon's chief secretary… -Ah, thank you for coming.

796
37:35.192 --> 37:36.151
…has also been acting

797
37:36.234 --> 37:38.028
-a little sketchy lately. -Oh, thanks a lot.

798
37:39.154 --> 37:40.906
Oh my, it's been a while.

799
37:40.989 --> 37:42.866
-[attendee] Yes, how have you been? -[camera shutters clicking]

800
37:43.617 --> 37:45.243
Long time no see, everyone.

801
37:45.744 --> 37:47.329
I hope you've all been keeping well.

802
37:47.412 --> 37:48.830
Oh, it's been so long.

803
37:49.831 --> 37:53.919
Uh, so I've brought, um, our own reporters today.

804
37:54.002 --> 37:55.378
[reporters] Hello.

805
37:55.879 --> 37:58.548
This is a good day, so let's all come together

806
37:59.257 --> 38:00.884
and write good news. You can do it.

807
38:00.967 --> 38:02.469
-[reporters] Yes, ma'am. -I'm counting on you all.

808
38:02.552 --> 38:03.845
[reporters] Yes, ma'am.

809
38:04.387 --> 38:06.389
Right. Well, you know what to do. Let's do it.

810
38:06.473 --> 38:07.474
[reporters] Yes, sir.

811
38:08.350 --> 38:10.519
Oh, I see you made it.

812
38:11.186 --> 38:13.063
Welcome. Thank you.

813
38:14.773 --> 38:16.650
-Oh, uh, you too, Mr. Moon. -[Mr. Moon] Oh, yes.

814
38:17.442 --> 38:18.944
[Wan-gu] Yoon Na-jung is the second child.

815
38:19.027 --> 38:20.862
That woman is infamous.

816
38:22.114 --> 38:23.824
They say she's a real piece of work.

817
38:24.449 --> 38:26.076
I met her at the family banquet,

818
38:26.493 --> 38:29.162
and Yoon Na-jung seemed to absolutely detest Yoon Yi-jun.

819
38:29.246 --> 38:30.997
Hmm…

820
38:31.081 --> 38:32.457
What about the eldest daughter?

821
38:32.541 --> 38:33.792
-Yoon Mi-jin? -Mm.

822
38:34.584 --> 38:36.002
Of the three Taekang children,

823
38:36.086 --> 38:39.047
they say her management style is closest to Chairman Yoon's,

824
38:39.131 --> 38:40.632
except she's nice.

825
38:40.715 --> 38:43.260
She's supportive of Yoon Yi-jun. She's selfless.

826
38:44.219 --> 38:45.971
If the succession war caused all this,

827
38:46.054 --> 38:48.014
does he get along with the rest of the family?

828
38:48.098 --> 38:49.224
The chief secretary?

829
38:49.307 --> 38:50.934
It seems he's been a good uncle.

830
38:51.017 --> 38:52.936
I mean, they're all his late older sister's children.

831
38:58.191 --> 38:59.317
[Wan-gu slurping]

832
39:11.496 --> 39:13.123
[reporter] Try smiling a bit more, everyone.

833
39:13.206 --> 39:14.499
-[camera shutters clicking] -Good.

834
39:14.583 --> 39:17.210
Okay, one, two, three.

835
39:17.294 --> 39:18.461
[redeemed inmates] Fighting!

836
39:22.132 --> 39:24.092
-[reporter] Okay, let's get another shot. -[sighs]

837
39:24.176 --> 39:26.052
[reporter] One, two…

838
39:26.136 --> 39:28.221
I know you're busy, so thanks for coming.

839
39:29.097 --> 39:30.599
It means a lot having you here.

840
39:31.183 --> 39:34.144
[Na-jung] The Taekang Foundation is our hotel's food catering VIP.

841
39:34.227 --> 39:36.938
-Of course I'm here. -Mm.

842
39:37.022 --> 39:38.565
[reporter] Now give me a heart, everyone.

843
39:38.648 --> 39:39.649
Yeah.

844
39:39.733 --> 39:42.068
But for an event being hosted under the Taekang name,

845
39:42.152 --> 39:44.112
it seems a bit drab.

846
39:44.196 --> 39:46.072
From now on, host it at our hotel.

847
39:46.156 --> 39:47.449
[reporter] Yes, very good.

848
39:47.532 --> 39:48.366
Huh?

849
39:49.159 --> 39:50.410
Would that be weird?

850
39:50.493 --> 39:54.539
Would our hotel be an awkward venue for your inmate integration project?

851
39:55.040 --> 39:56.416
-[chuckles] -[Na-jung laughs]

852
39:58.084 --> 40:00.003
A lot of care went into this event.

853
40:00.503 --> 40:02.088
I'd appreciate your support.

854
40:02.172 --> 40:03.298
Well, why not?

855
40:03.840 --> 40:05.800
It is the only event of yours that's taken off

856
40:05.884 --> 40:08.094
since Father handed the foundation to you.

857
40:08.178 --> 40:10.597
-[chuckles] -I'm sure you could use the support.

858
40:10.680 --> 40:12.515
[both laugh]

859
40:13.141 --> 40:15.518
I'll let the chairman know you dropped by and put in a good word.

860
40:15.602 --> 40:17.938
Oh, you don't have to go to all the hassle.

861
40:18.313 --> 40:19.856
I manage fine on my own.

862
40:21.650 --> 40:24.319
Why do you think I dragged all this dead weight along with me?

863
40:25.946 --> 40:28.573
[Mr. Moon] Sir, I think we want more shots of them smiling.

864
40:29.324 --> 40:30.492
In high school,

865
40:30.575 --> 40:34.412
I kept coming in second every year because of this one bitch.

866
40:35.580 --> 40:37.082
What do you think I did?

867
40:38.541 --> 40:41.044
Uh, well, um, given your personality,

868
40:41.711 --> 40:43.046
I'm sure you tried harder.

869
40:43.546 --> 40:44.839
I did try harder.

870
40:45.674 --> 40:47.425
I drugged that bitch's food, you see.

871
40:47.509 --> 40:49.094
[ominous music playing]

872
40:49.177 --> 40:51.721
[chuckling]

873
40:51.805 --> 40:54.808
That was the first time my father praised me, and I thought…

874
40:54.891 --> 40:56.309
[gasps] "Oh…

875
40:57.018 --> 40:59.312
you just need to take what you want

876
41:00.188 --> 41:02.274
by any means possible

877
41:03.316 --> 41:04.651
yourself."

878
41:05.235 --> 41:09.197
[laughing]

879
41:10.365 --> 41:12.867
-[laughing continues] -[awkward chuckle]

880
41:16.371 --> 41:17.414
Park Min-hwan…

881
41:19.040 --> 41:19.874
where is he?

882
41:22.085 --> 41:22.919
[scoffs]

883
41:24.129 --> 41:26.089
He's gonna ruffle a lot of feathers

884
41:26.172 --> 41:28.383
once people find out what he's made off with.

885
41:28.466 --> 41:29.426
Don't you think so?

886
41:30.302 --> 41:31.303
You could be right.

887
41:32.679 --> 41:34.055
I can't help wondering

888
41:34.139 --> 41:36.725
if some of those feathers happen to be yours, Ms. Yoon.

889
41:39.894 --> 41:42.272
[laughing]

890
41:43.023 --> 41:45.608
[laughing continues]

891
41:46.985 --> 41:50.280
Man, I'm a pretty good judge of character,

892
41:50.822 --> 41:52.574
but your character eludes me.

893
41:55.493 --> 41:58.163
Whether you're aligned with Yoon Yi-jun, the chairman,

894
41:58.955 --> 42:00.040
or with me…

895
42:03.418 --> 42:04.753
it's time to choose.

896
42:11.051 --> 42:11.885
Here's the deal.

897
42:11.968 --> 42:13.636
If you bring Park Min-hwan to me…

898
42:15.889 --> 42:17.932
then I'll tell you what you're dying to know.

899
42:23.605 --> 42:25.357
I'm not running a charity here.

900
42:26.900 --> 42:28.109
Give and take.

901
42:36.451 --> 42:38.411
[clicking on phone]

902
42:42.082 --> 42:42.999
[phone chimes]

903
42:55.303 --> 42:57.639
So, Ms. Han had two mobile phones?

904
42:57.722 --> 42:59.891
What do you think? Why do the cops want it?

905
42:59.974 --> 43:01.851
I guess they think there must be something in it.

906
43:02.685 --> 43:03.895
Where could it be?

907
43:05.105 --> 43:07.565
-If someone took that phone, then… -[sighs]

908
43:07.649 --> 43:09.359
You worried someone else might end up dead?

909
43:11.236 --> 43:12.862
Should you worry about others right now?

910
43:14.072 --> 43:15.740
[glass tinkling]

911
43:17.450 --> 43:20.078
[glass shattering]

912
43:22.038 --> 43:24.874
I'll do whatever it takes to prevent any further damage.

913
43:25.625 --> 43:27.252
By the way, about Mr. Park…

914
43:29.963 --> 43:31.297
is he somewhere safe?

915
43:36.177 --> 43:39.264
[Jae-hee] Seok-jin, can you please find out

916
43:39.347 --> 43:41.266
where the herbicide in the milk came from?

917
43:41.349 --> 43:42.976
[store owner] Well, it pretty much kills everything.

918
43:43.059 --> 43:44.519
Animals, plants.

919
43:52.986 --> 43:54.571
BUSINESS REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE BOWOON CHEMICAL CO., LTD

920
43:59.534 --> 44:01.453
[Si-a] Hi, Jessica.

921
44:02.495 --> 44:04.122
Can you do me a favor?

922
44:04.205 --> 44:07.250
Could you bring me a surprise gift for Yoon Yi-jun?

923
44:08.251 --> 44:10.170
-Hmm. -[phone beeps]

924
44:10.253 --> 44:13.298
Only when an item finds its rightful owner

925
44:13.840 --> 44:16.217
does it reveal its true value, after all.

926
44:18.970 --> 44:21.806
[soft gasp]

927
44:22.932 --> 44:24.309
[irritated groan]

928
44:24.392 --> 44:25.226
[sighs]

929
44:25.310 --> 44:26.936
The readability is poor.

930
44:27.020 --> 44:27.854
Do it again.

931
44:27.937 --> 44:29.481
[yells] Again! Again!

932
44:29.564 --> 44:30.440
[papers rustling]

933
44:30.982 --> 44:32.066
[annoyed groan]

934
44:32.150 --> 44:33.359
[inhales deeply]

935
44:33.443 --> 44:35.695
He's like an evil little stepmother.

936
44:36.863 --> 44:38.448
[inhales deeply]

937
44:38.531 --> 44:40.617
[exhales deeply]

938
44:42.118 --> 44:43.369
[tapping on desk]

939
44:43.453 --> 44:45.747
Ugh, that's not important right now.

940
44:57.800 --> 44:58.968
[clattering]

941
44:59.761 --> 45:01.721
-[door opens] -Oh, ooh, it just…

942
45:01.804 --> 45:02.639
[door closes]

943
45:02.722 --> 45:04.474
What? What… What is it? What now?

944
45:04.557 --> 45:07.352
It's just… The desk just went, "Oof," by itself.

945
45:07.810 --> 45:08.645
Just fell apart.

946
45:10.104 --> 45:11.439
Give me a second.

947
45:12.148 --> 45:13.816
-[Da-woon grunts] -[rattling]

948
45:14.651 --> 45:16.027
Your desk is acting up too?

949
45:16.486 --> 45:17.487
[sighs]

950
45:18.488 --> 45:19.405
What should I do?

951
45:20.073 --> 45:21.324
-[sighs] -[clicking on phone]

952
45:24.077 --> 45:26.079
Click the link I just sent to get a new one.

953
45:26.579 --> 45:27.747
The partner center will reach out.

954
45:28.498 --> 45:29.624
Cool. Thanks for that.

955
45:35.004 --> 45:37.549
STRATEGY TF TEAM MANAGING DIRECTOR'S SECRETARY'S OFFICE

956
45:37.632 --> 45:38.508
SECRETARY'S OFFICE DESK REPLACEMENT REQUEST

957
45:39.217 --> 45:40.134
[Jae-hee] Hmm?

958
45:40.218 --> 45:42.845
Someone filed a request for a replacement desk?

959
45:44.472 --> 45:45.557
Who could it be?

960
45:46.641 --> 45:48.184
SEOK-JIN

961
45:48.268 --> 45:50.103
-[inhales, clears throat] -[phone buzzing]

962
45:57.318 --> 45:58.736
[buzzing continues]

963
45:59.654 --> 46:00.488
Yes, Seok-jin.

964
46:00.572 --> 46:02.240
Have you heard of Bowoon Chemical?

965
46:02.323 --> 46:03.866
Bowoon Chemical?

966
46:03.950 --> 46:06.244
It's the sole importer of herbicide ingredients here.

967
46:06.327 --> 46:07.996
It's part of Taekang Chemical.

968
46:08.538 --> 46:09.539
Get this…

969
46:10.665 --> 46:12.584
Yoon Na-jung also manages Taekang Chemical.

970
46:13.376 --> 46:14.294
[soft gasp]

971
46:16.170 --> 46:17.255
Yoon Na-jung does?

972
46:29.100 --> 46:32.520
[tense music playing]

973
46:37.775 --> 46:38.943
Are you afraid…

974
46:41.195 --> 46:42.822
someone might end up dead?

975
46:46.951 --> 46:48.244
[breathes shakily]

976
46:50.538 --> 46:51.539
[grunts, groans]

977
46:51.623 --> 46:55.126
[breathing heavily]

978
47:06.638 --> 47:07.764
[gasps]

979
47:07.847 --> 47:10.516
[music swells]

980
47:11.851 --> 47:15.938
Herbicide made by Taekang Chemical, overseen by Yoon Na-jung…

981
47:17.357 --> 47:19.901
Kim Si-hyun is the one who delivers the milk…

982
47:21.319 --> 47:25.073
And the late-night meeting between Kim Si-hyun and Yoon Na-jung…

983
47:26.199 --> 47:27.825
[sighs] Kim Si-hyun…

984
47:33.790 --> 47:34.832
[thumps]

985
47:38.127 --> 47:40.129
[tense music playing]

986
47:48.262 --> 47:49.389
[panting]

987
47:49.472 --> 47:50.973
Sorry, sir. Are you okay?

988
47:51.057 --> 47:52.350
[both panting]

989
47:52.433 --> 47:54.060
[gasps]

990
47:54.143 --> 47:55.937
-[soft music playing] -[heart pounding]

991
47:59.524 --> 48:02.360
[jaunty music playing from toy]

992
48:04.946 --> 48:06.656
Holy crap!

993
48:06.739 --> 48:07.949
[gasps]

994
48:08.408 --> 48:10.076
-Am I a monster? -[Jae-hee] Oh…

995
48:12.203 --> 48:14.122
Did you mistake me for an armed thug?

996
48:14.205 --> 48:15.873
Please excuse me. I apologize.

997
48:22.714 --> 48:24.924
Actually, I quite like you, Mr. Kang.

998
48:26.384 --> 48:28.177
I find you so refreshing.

999
48:32.432 --> 48:33.683
Can I have your number?

1000
48:35.184 --> 48:36.018
Oppa.

1001
48:36.102 --> 48:37.061
[gasps]

1002
48:39.897 --> 48:40.898
Give it to her.

1003
48:47.029 --> 48:48.322
I wanna hit you up every day.

1004
48:48.406 --> 48:49.407
Can I?

1005
48:49.490 --> 48:51.451
-No, don't. -Do it if you want.

1006
48:51.993 --> 48:53.369
[Si-a] Hmm…

1007
48:54.412 --> 48:57.331
Well, since you guys can't agree, I'll just do what I want, okay?

1008
49:00.918 --> 49:03.463
Use this to play with Jerry. You two should get along.

1009
49:05.047 --> 49:07.049
Right. Let's go out. You're hungry, right?

1010
49:07.717 --> 49:09.761
[Si-a] Mm-hmm. Buy me some meat.

1011
49:09.844 --> 49:11.345
I want it cooked rare…

1012
49:12.972 --> 49:14.098
and still bloody.

1013
49:17.143 --> 49:18.436
[sighs]

1014
49:18.519 --> 49:19.437
[Da-woon] What did he say?

1015
49:19.520 --> 49:21.814
He tell you to resign? Did he threaten to fire you?

1016
49:22.523 --> 49:24.275
No. Well, not exactly…

1017
49:24.358 --> 49:26.778
You mistook his fiancée for a thug after all, so…

1018
49:28.070 --> 49:29.071
I'll help you.

1019
49:29.614 --> 49:30.865
I'll let him know.

1020
49:30.948 --> 49:33.618
I'll get you retrained and then beg for your mercy.

1021
49:35.787 --> 49:36.954
[Da-woon gasps]

1022
49:39.791 --> 49:40.875
You're not needed.

1023
49:41.501 --> 49:42.418
Don't follow me.

1024
49:50.009 --> 49:51.177
Let's be friends, huh?

1025
49:51.803 --> 49:53.012
I'll call you. Hmm.

1026
49:56.849 --> 49:58.518
You must be shaken, so go home early.

1027
49:58.601 --> 50:00.269
-I'll go with Mr. Yoon. -[door closes]

1028
50:06.984 --> 50:09.487
I haven't had a dopamine hit like this in a while.

1029
50:09.570 --> 50:11.030
[breathes sharply]

1030
50:12.657 --> 50:14.575
Things are about to get more interesting.

1031
50:20.039 --> 50:21.457
[elevator dings]

1032
50:21.541 --> 50:23.376
[elevator doors open]

1033
50:25.545 --> 50:27.713
[Yi-jun] You're not needed. Don't follow me.

1034
50:27.797 --> 50:28.923
-[knocking on door] -[door opens]

1035
50:30.550 --> 50:31.676
You need a desk replaced?

1036
50:32.218 --> 50:33.427
Yes, this one here.

1037
50:33.928 --> 50:34.929
[employee] Let's go.

1038
50:39.308 --> 50:41.811
-[desk clattering] -[employee grunts]

1039
50:42.311 --> 50:43.938
-Thanks a lot. -You're welcome.

1040
50:57.702 --> 50:58.703
[phone buzzes]

1041
51:00.538 --> 51:02.290
[Jae-hee] They just left with the desk.

1042
51:02.373 --> 51:04.166
Okay.

1043
51:06.168 --> 51:07.128
[employee grunts]

1044
51:10.006 --> 51:11.799
Oh, good work, guys.

1045
51:12.383 --> 51:14.051
I went over the logs, and it's been a while

1046
51:14.135 --> 51:15.219
since we cleaned in here.

1047
51:15.303 --> 51:16.679
Since I'm here,

1048
51:16.762 --> 51:18.556
I might as well clean the floor, am I right?

1049
51:18.639 --> 51:19.849
Yes, well, sure, why not?

1050
51:19.932 --> 51:20.766
[soft chuckle]

1051
51:20.850 --> 51:22.351
Just make sure to shut the door when you're done.

1052
51:22.435 --> 51:23.644
Of course. Don't worry.

1053
51:23.728 --> 51:25.313
-[Wan-gu] Take care. -[employee] Yep.

1054
51:34.405 --> 51:35.573
[Young-sook and Young-chun] Bin!

1055
51:37.950 --> 51:40.286
[Young-sook] Binney! Get over here!

1056
51:40.369 --> 51:41.579
[Wan-gu sighs]

1057
51:41.662 --> 51:43.539
[Wan-gu] Yes, I'm coming.

1058
51:45.124 --> 51:47.376
[low suspenseful music playing]

1059
51:56.510 --> 51:57.720
Let's see.

1060
52:11.901 --> 52:12.777
Huh?

1061
52:15.988 --> 52:17.990
The product number is…

1062
52:18.074 --> 52:19.408
807…

1063
52:20.242 --> 52:22.036
TKKSO.

1064
52:27.124 --> 52:29.919
APPLICANT NAME

1065
52:30.002 --> 52:31.128
"Lee Hye-jung"?

1066
52:53.275 --> 52:54.276
Are you hungry?

1067
52:56.988 --> 52:57.989
I'm hungry.

1068
53:10.668 --> 53:11.502
Not there.

1069
53:26.017 --> 53:27.351
-[device beeps] -Huh?

1070
53:27.977 --> 53:30.563
[rhythmic suspenseful music playing]

1071
53:32.690 --> 53:33.607
It's not here.

1072
53:35.609 --> 53:36.444
[beeping]

1073
53:42.867 --> 53:43.951
[strained grunt]

1074
53:46.495 --> 53:47.955
-[rattles] -[gasps]

1075
53:50.416 --> 53:51.500
Oh.

1076
53:52.543 --> 53:54.170
[rattling]

1077
53:57.840 --> 53:59.091
[gasps]

1078
54:01.427 --> 54:02.595
[inhales]

1079
54:05.347 --> 54:06.265
Oppa.

1080
54:07.767 --> 54:09.977
If you leave your food untouched,

1081
54:11.062 --> 54:12.104
you'll go to hell.

1082
54:13.731 --> 54:15.149
Let's just walk in silence.

1083
54:19.111 --> 54:20.321
Your complexion,

1084
54:20.404 --> 54:22.782
it's very much a basement level three tone,

1085
54:23.365 --> 54:25.034
which brings me to my point.

1086
54:26.160 --> 54:27.369
I want us to get married.

1087
54:28.204 --> 54:29.580
As soon as possible.

1088
54:29.663 --> 54:31.165
It's perfect timing, no?

1089
54:33.167 --> 54:35.961
And that means I'm going to need you to cooperate with me.

1090
54:37.963 --> 54:39.548
As for the announcement date,

1091
54:39.632 --> 54:41.175
choose whenever you want,

1092
54:41.258 --> 54:42.635
around the shareholder meeting.

1093
54:43.260 --> 54:45.387
Whatever works for you. Hmm.

1094
54:49.016 --> 54:51.102
[pensive music playing]

1095
54:52.394 --> 54:53.395
[sighs]

1096
54:55.981 --> 54:58.359
Special Forces, what about dinner?

1097
54:58.859 --> 54:59.860
Uh, sir?

1098
55:02.613 --> 55:05.116
Special Forces' dinner. Did he eat?

1099
55:05.658 --> 55:07.159
I did make sure he had dinner,

1100
55:07.993 --> 55:10.162
and I made sure to grab myself some cup noodles too.

1101
55:12.081 --> 55:13.082
I see.

1102
55:15.626 --> 55:16.627
[sighs]

1103
55:21.841 --> 55:23.843
[gentle poignant music playing]

1104
55:41.318 --> 55:42.570
[sighs]

1105
55:47.658 --> 55:49.618
Man, I really hope we can get something out of this.

1106
55:49.702 --> 55:52.329
The captain's gonna give it to forensics. We'll have to wait.

1107
55:52.413 --> 55:55.624
I'm gonna bail from this place the moment we catch the killer.

1108
55:56.458 --> 55:58.294
I heard it's been hard. Can you manage it?

1109
55:58.377 --> 56:01.297
[sighs] Do you have any idea how heartless he is?

1110
56:01.380 --> 56:02.882
I work hard for his safety.

1111
56:02.965 --> 56:05.176
He won't let me near him now. And… [sighs]

1112
56:07.178 --> 56:08.512
I guess if you think about it,

1113
56:09.221 --> 56:10.347
I'm worse than he is,

1114
56:11.182 --> 56:12.766
'cause I'll end up stabbing him in the back.

1115
56:14.435 --> 56:17.229
One day, when he finds out who I am…

1116
56:17.980 --> 56:20.191
Yoon Yi-jun will think I betrayed him, right?

1117
56:23.986 --> 56:25.237
[breathes heavily]

1118
56:26.363 --> 56:27.198
Kang Jae-hee!

1119
56:30.201 --> 56:32.995
Seok-jin, you should head back first.

1120
56:43.839 --> 56:46.217
Sir, didn't you say you were heading out for a meal?

1121
56:50.512 --> 56:53.557
This is important. I need to double-check something.

1122
56:54.600 --> 56:55.434
Huh?

1123
56:56.977 --> 56:58.312
You're the one who started it, though.

1124
57:04.109 --> 57:05.444
[twinkling effect]

1125
57:06.862 --> 57:09.531
[soft music playing]

1126
57:21.043 --> 57:23.295
[Jae-hee] You did. You looked out for me.

1127
57:23.379 --> 57:26.840
[Yi-jun] Why are you noticing the things I don't want anyone to know?

1128
58:10.843 --> 58:12.845
[handcuffs rattling, click]

1129
58:14.847 --> 58:17.766
[closing theme music playing]

1130
58:36.910 --> 58:38.787
SPECIAL THANKS TO CHOI HEE-JIN AND JUNG YOO-MIN

1131
58:38.871 --> 58:40.456
[Si-hyun] What's so good about Mr. Kang?

1132
58:40.539 --> 58:41.373
Oh, sorry.

1133
58:41.457 --> 58:42.958
You like him, right? [chuckles]

1134
58:43.042 --> 58:44.043
[yells] I…

1135
58:44.126 --> 58:45.336
He's going to be the president.

1136
58:45.419 --> 58:46.879
[Tae-sik] Announce it before the shareholder meeting.

1137
58:46.962 --> 58:49.548
About Yi-jun's new personal secretary, give him to me.

1138
58:49.631 --> 58:51.342
[Yi-jun] It made no sense to begin with.

1139
58:51.425 --> 58:53.135
Of all the emotions to get wrong…

1140
58:53.218 --> 58:56.555
Strange rumors have been going around about you and Ms. Yoon Na-jung.

1141
58:56.638 --> 58:58.891
[Hye-jung] Actually, I approached you on purpose, Mr. Kim.

1142
58:58.974 --> 59:02.144
[Si-hyun] Isn't it a bit strange that Mr. Kang's been acting on his own?

1143
59:02.227 --> 59:03.604
Please, just stick to my orders!

1144
59:03.687 --> 59:05.105
[Jae-hee] I was wrong about you.

1145
59:05.189 --> 59:06.940
I thought you were a decent person.
